# ADU-REPO-01 §3 — ownership
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so order matters: the broad workstream
# rules come first and the shared paths that need two reviewers come last.
#
# An unassigned path has no owner line and gets a review from whoever is nearest
# until it does. That is deliberate: an owner invented for an unstaffed workstream
# is a review that nobody actually performs.

/apps/api/          @naod
/db/                @naod
/contracts/         @naod
/ops/               @naod
/docs/              @naod

/apps/console/      @abenezer

# /apps/mobile/     — unassigned (ADU-REPO-01 §1)
# /apps/storefront/ — unassigned (ADU-REPO-01 §1)

# Both owners. A change here reaches every workstream, which is the whole reason
# `packages/` exists — see §4 rule 2. The correct way past a dependency rule is to
# move the shared thing here, and that move is meant to be a deliberate, reviewed
# act rather than a convenience.
/packages/          @naod @abenezer
/.github/           @naod @abenezer
/CLAUDE.md          @naod @abenezer
